cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to Genoryn Krypton, please cite it as below."
title: "Genoryn Krypton: quantum-resistant, private-by-default proof-of-work cryptocurrency"
abstract: >-
  Genoryn Krypton (GNR) is a proof-of-work cryptocurrency with Bitcoin's monetary design
  (21,000,000 coins, halvings every 2,100,000 blocks, fair launch, no premine) whose funds
  and privacy depend on no elliptic curve: spends are zk-STARK proofs over hash functions,
  every transfer is shielded, notes are encrypted with hybrid X25519 + ML-KEM-1024, mining
  rewards are shared by every miner in proportion to its work, light clients verify the
  chain with Merkle Mountain Range proofs, and GNR is exchanged with bitcoin through atomic
  swaps.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "Zarazi Sokani"
repository-code: "https://github.com/genoryn/genoryn"
url: "https://genoryn.io"
license:
